<title>UK: British gas to be hit by customer defections-paper.</title>
<headline>British gas to be hit by customer defections-paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>One in eight gas customers in the British counties of Kent and Sussex, the latest pilot areas for competition, has contracted to switch supplier away from British Gas to other suppliers, The Times newspaper said on Friday.</p>
<p>The paper said Transco, the British Gas company that runs gas pipelines, said that 112,375 out of 900,000 customers in the two counties have asked to desert Centrica, British Gas' supply arm.</p>
<p>Most defectors have been signed up by Scottish Power and Beacon Gas, the paper said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7715</p>
